127:Tf32,*Waldems, October 2024* – plastship GmbH invites you to register for the [**4th International Recycling Forum**](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/) on **December 10–11, 2024**, at the **Dorint Hotel in Wiesbaden**. Organized by [RIGK](https://www.rigk.de/en/)and [EPRO](https://epro-plasticscircularity.org/), this event brings together international experts to drive the future of plastics recycling. The forum offers hands-on insights, top-notch networking opportunities, and concrete case studies – an opportunity you won’t want to miss!

## Why you shouldn’t miss the recycling forum:

The event features an exciting [agenda](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/agenda)with high-profile [speakers](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/speakers-1)who are industry experts, delivering the latest circular economy topics in a dynamic, hands-on way, including:

- **Market trends and the circular economy** – Discover the latest developments and innovations shaping the market and the circular economy.
- **Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR)** – Practical solutions and new models for assuming responsibility along the value chain.
- **AI and Digitalization** – Insights into how digitalization and AI are optimizing recycling efficiency and quality.
- **Complementary recycling technologies** – Opportunities and challenges in combining chemical and mechanical recycling methods for sustainable raw material recovery.
- **PPWR session** – Key regulatory updates and their impacts on the plastics industry.
- **Technical innovations** – Showcasing the latest technologies to make recycling processes more efficient and versatile.
- **Agricultural plastics recycling** – Solutions and practical examples tailored specifically to the agricultural sector.
- **Panel discussions and Q&A sessions** – Your chance to ask questions and engage in conversations with industry experts.

## Networking in an elegant setting

The event offers not only professional insights but also excellent networking opportunities. A special highlight is the evening event on the second day at the historic Kurhaus Wiesbaden, providing a relaxed atmosphere to connect with industry colleagues and partners.

[Learn more](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/evening-event)

![](/images/cms/wiesbadener-kurhaus-fotolia-71847068-l-1bcf60.webp)

## Exclusive networking – plastship and partners on-site

Visit the exhibitor area to meet plastship and our partners [3S, Veridis, and RAM](/partners/), who will showcase their latest recycling solutions. Discover innovations and gain inspiration to further advance your own business goals in the circular economy.

[All exhibitors and sponsors](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/exhibitors)

![](/images/cms/srgdaega-fa55d6.webp)

## Andreas Bastian, founder of plastship, on the Forum:

> The International Recycling Forum is a unique platform to discuss the latest developments and challenges in plastics recycling, For us, it is a special opportunity to exchange ideas with international experts and work together on innovative solutions for a sustainable circular economy. We look forward to advancing progress in plastics recycling with the participants.

The Recycling Forum is your chance to learn directly from industry leaders, build valuable connections, and strengthen your company’s goals in sustainability and the circular economy. Registration is now open, and spaces are limited. Don’t miss this exclusive opportunity!

[**Register now – Become part of the circular future!**](https://www.international-recycling-forum.de/en/registration)

If you have questions or suggestions, please contact me!

**Mirco Gattinger**, Marketing & Social Media Manager\
